    "summary": "High‑energy Dark Star trek and soaring Sugar Magnolia",
    "blurb": "The show features a soaring Dark Star jam, crisp Sugar Magnolia, and an inspired Good Lovin' finish. Jerry’s jazzy guitar and Bill’s standout drum solo drive the high‑energy second set, while Keith’s organ adds West‑Coast texture. The recording quality is excellent throughout.",
    "review": "May 4, 1972 at the Olympia Theater in Paris captures one of the most electrifying moments of the Europe ’72 tour. From the opening set’s tight blues romp into a blistering Dark Star that stretches across two halves with Bill Kreutzmann delivering one of his finest drum solos, the band never loses its groove. Jerry Garcia’s wah‑infused leads soar over Keith Godchaux’s angelic organ, especially on The Stranger (Two Souls in Communion) and the climactic Sugar Magnolia. Bob Weir’s vocals lift Good Lovin' and Jack Straw to new heights, while Phil Lesh’s rumbling bass underpins the spacey improvisations. The Miller soundboard capture preserves every nuance with a clean, crisp mix that makes this performance feel both immediate and timeless.",
